    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d500">

                <pb facs="0660" n="564" xml:id="pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/2833: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-02T09:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                                1921—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:18 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>128. The President’s private secretary Aguirre Muñoz leaves to-day on special
                    mission to assure Nicaraguan Government that Honduranean Government will make
                    every effort to prevent further disturbances on the frontier.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
